steps.text:
**Confirming cellular behavior:** Yes, turning off cellular is the intended behavior. In `setting.py`, the `set_low_battery_mode_status` function explicitly disables all three dependent services when low-battery mode is turned on:

```python
if on:
    for dependent_setting in ["cellular", "wifi", "location_service"]:
        try:
            set_boolean_settings(dependent_setting, on=False)
        except ValueError:
            pass
```

Additionally, re-enabling any of those services while low-battery mode is on is blocked by `PermissionError` checks in each setter (`set_cellular_service_status`, `set_wifi_status`, `set_location_service_status`). So this is fully intentional.

